Third-party components -- READ THIS BEFORE DISTRIBUTING
-------------------------------------------------------
This repository interacts with components whose licenses constrain distribution.
Getting this wrong is the single most likely licensing mistake in the project.

  librqbit        Apache-2.0    -- BitTorrent engine (madde 1)
  mpv / libmpv    LGPL-2.1+     -- when built with --lgpl
                  GPL-2.0+      -- as commonly distributed, with GPL-only
                                   components or a GPL-configured FFmpeg
  FFmpeg          LGPL-2.1+ or GPL-2.0+ depending on build configuration

Consequences:
  * A GPL-configured mpv/FFmpeg build requires the distributed binary to be
    GPL-compatible. GPL-3.0-or-later satisfies this; a permissive-only license
    would not.
  * v1 runs mpv as a SEPARATE PROCESS over JSON IPC (madde 2). This keeps the
    coupling weak. If libmpv is ever embedded in-process, revisit this file and
    the app's bundling before shipping.
  * Redistributing mpv or FFmpeg binaries carries their own source-availability
    obligations. Build inputs and exact configure flags must be recorded in
    `docs/third-party-builds.md` before any release that bundles them.
